# Schafe koennen sicher weiden (Sheep may safely graze), aria from the
# Hunting Cantata "Was mir behagt, ist nur die muntre Jagd", BWV 208
# (J. S. Bach)
#
# Movement 9, sung by Pales, goddess of shepherds, at a birthday
# celebration for Duke Christian of Saxe-Weissenfels (1713): sheep graze
# safely where a good shepherd watches; where rulers govern well, there
# is peace. Two recorders (flutes in this edition), soprano and continuo.
#
# Character: a pastorale in B-flat major, calm and tender. The two flutes
# play in thirds over a continuo of steady repeated eighths, like a
# shepherd's drone; the soprano sings long, gentle phrases. The flute
# figures carry Bach's own echo marks (p and f within the bar).
#
# Time signature: 4/4, 40 bars in the Mutopia score (Breitkopf, 1881)
# and in the MIDI; the first note is on the downbeat.
#
# Form: da capo aria. A = bars 1-21 (ritornello, the voice, ritornello),
# ending on the downbeat of bar 21 with a fermata (the Fine); B = bars
# 21-40, starting on that same downbeat and ending on F, the dominant,
# where the score says "Da Capo". The MIDI plays the 40 bars once, so the
# da capo is written out with `play`: bars 1-40, then 1 to the fermata
# quarter of bar 21. That last quarter also holds the voice's first B
# note (D, a tone of the B-flat chord), which is harmless.
#
# Parts: track 1 flute 1, track 2 flute 2, track 3 soprano (Pales),
# track 4 continuo (checked against the score: the soprano enters in
# bar 5, the continuo opens on repeated B-flats). Four parts on three
# channels: with `parts 3 4 1 2` the soprano and the bass always sound,
# then flute 1, and flute 2 gives way when all four play.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 56. As performed (with the da capo) it is about 60
# bars, 241 quarters. MusicBrainz track times for sung recordings with
# period or chamber forces: Joanne Lunn, Bach Collegium Japan, Suzuki
# 4:29, about 54; Gillian Fisher, King's Consort 4:25, about 55; Sara
# Macliver, Orchestra of the Antipodes 4:34, about 53; Susanne Ryden,
# Voices of Music 4:15, about 57; Magdalena Kozena, Musica Florea 4:05,
# about 59; Lynne Dawson 4:00, about 60; Nuria Rial 3:50, about 63.
# Slower: Arleen Auger with Schreier 5:52; Elisabeth Schwarzkopf 1946,
# 4:58 (bach-cantatas.com). These conversions assume the full da capo;
# I did not check each recording for cuts. 56 sits with Suzuki, King
# and Ryden: a walking pastorale, not a dirge, with the 32nd-note flute
# turns still clear (about 8 frames each).
#
# Structure (score bars; my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   1-4    ritornello, flutes in thirds; echo marks in bars 3-4
#   5-8    the voice alone with continuo: "Schafe koennen sicher weiden,
#          wo ein guter Hirte wacht", cadence in F (bar 8)
#   9-16   flutes and voice together, then flute echoes in the gaps
#          (11-12); cadence in B-flat (bars 16-17)
#   17-21  ritornello again with its echoes (19-20); Fine at bar 21
#   21-26  B: "Wo Regenten wohl regieren", G minor to C minor (26)
#   26-30  ritornello figures in C minor, echo marks in 29-30
#   30-40  the voice again, through D minor and G minor ("Ruh' und
#          Frieden"), the long melismas, to the half close on F (40)
#
# Bars as performed (after `play`):
#   bars 1-40 as in the score; the da capo is bars 41-61.25 (score bar x
#   is 40+x).
#
# Plan: A at mf with the score's echoes taken literally (each marked p
# half-bar at mp); B, the minor-key middle, a step softer, coming back
# to mf for its last phrase into the half close, which broadens before
# the da capo. The da capo as the first time; a gentle final ritardando
# through the closing echoes. The continuo's low B-flats (below B2) are
# lifted an octave by the converter; the bass sits higher than written
# in the opening and closing ritornellos.

tempo 56
parts 3 4 1 2
play 1-40 1-21.25

voice mid 1        # the mid voice is mostly flute 2 or flute 1 under the
                   # soprano: keep it a step behind the outer lines

dyn 1 mf           # A: ritornello
dyn 3.5 mp         # echo marks (score bars 3-4: p, f, p)
dyn 4 mf
dyn 4.5 mp
dyn 5 mf           # the voice enters
dyn 19.5 mp        # the closing ritornello's echoes (19-20)
dyn 20 mf
dyn 20.5 mp
dyn 21 mp          # B: "Wo Regenten", the minor-key middle
dyn 29 p           # echo marks in the C minor ritornello (29: p, f)
dyn 29.5 mp
dyn 30 mp          # the voice returns
dyn 35 mf          # the last phrase, to the half close on F

dyn 41 mf          # da capo: as the first time
dyn 43.5 mp
dyn 44 mf
dyn 44.5 mp
dyn 45 mf
dyn 59.5 mp
dyn 60 mf
dyn 60.5 mp

broaden 8 0.95     # the voice's first cadence, in F
broaden 16 0.94    # cadence in B-flat, end of the vocal section
broaden 26 0.94    # cadence in C minor
broaden 40 0.88    # the half close on F: a breath before the da capo
broaden 48 0.95    # da capo: as bars 8 and 16
broaden 56 0.94

rit 2 0.75         # the closing echoes and the final B-flat
